# Line-ending policy for this repository.
#
# History: the 2024 upstream/ICCE-TW-era sources (pixelsnail.py, vqvae.py, dataset.py,
# train_vqvae.py, train_pixelsnail.py, ...) were committed with CRLF endings, while every
# 2026 ICETA-era script is LF. The .py files were normalised to LF in the pre-publication
# cleanup; this file keeps them that way and stops the two conventions diverging again.

# Default: treat as text, normalise to LF in the index and on checkout.
* text=auto eol=lf

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# EXCEPTION — results/*.csv must NEVER be renormalised.
#
# These manifests are written by Python's csv module with newline='' (see
# build_split.py, make_tight_crops.py, make_budget_subsamples.py), which emits \r\n by
# construction. They are audited data artefacts: their exact bytes back the board-split
# and subsample provenance recorded in AUDIT.md. Rewriting their line endings would
# change 25k+ lines and invalidate that byte-level trail for no benefit — Python's csv
# reader handles either convention transparently.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
results/*.csv -text

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Binary: never diff, never touch line endings.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.pt    binary
*.pth   binary
*.npy   binary
*.mdb   binary
*.zip   binary
*.pdf   binary
